+# Review: After Framework Application
+
+> This is the 0-120 scorecard result for `examples/01-saas-landing/after/`, generated by following the AI Design Engineer framework end-to-end.
+
+## Scorecard
+
+| # | Category | Score | Notes |
+|---|----------|-------|-------|
+| 1 | UX & IA | **14/15** | Hero CTA above fold, journey is obvious, pricing clear. Could add a "Watch demo" secondary CTA. |
+| 2 | Visual Design & Hierarchy | **13/15** | Strong typographic hierarchy (Cal Sans display vs Inter body). H2 in some sections is only slightly larger than H3. |
+| 3 | Design System Compliance | **14/15** | All colors via `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`. Spacing follows 8px scale. Components from shadcn/ui. |
+| 4 | Code Quality | **13/15** | Strict TS, components < 200 lines, content lifted to `lib/content.ts`. One `useEffect` for FAQ state could be simpler. |
+| 5 | Accessibility | **13/15** | Skip-to-content link, ARIA labels on icon buttons, focus traps in mobile menu and dialog. Contrast passes WCAG AA. Pricing toggle announces state. |
+| 6 | Performance | **13/15** | All images via `next/image`, fonts via `next/font`, no client-side data fetching. Could add `loading="lazy"` to below-fold images. |
+| 7 | Responsive Design | **14/15** | Tested at 320, 375, 768, 1024, 1440. Mobile menu has focus trap. Touch targets ≥ 44px. |
+| 8 | Production Readiness | **13/15** | Meta tags complete, OG image set, no console.log, error boundary in place. Could add structured data (JSON-LD). |
+| **Total** | | **107/120** | 🏆 **Production-ready** |
+
+## Verdict: 107/120 — 🏆 Ship it
+
+This is the result you get when you use the framework end-to-end. Compare to the **before** version which scored **46/120** — same AI, different process.
+
+## Top 3 polish items (optional)
+
+- 🟢 Add JSON-LD structured data for the SaaS product
+- 🟢 Add subtle scroll-reveal animation (with `prefers-reduced-motion` fallback)
+- 🟢 A/B test hero copy: "Ship features your users actually want" vs current
+
+## Comparison
+
+| Metric | Before | After | Delta |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Score | 46/120 | 107/120 | **+61 (+132%)** |
+| Production-ready | ❌ | ✅ | — |
+| Accessibility | 4/15 | 13/15 | +9 |
+| Design system | 3/15 | 14/15 | +11 |
+| Code quality | 7/15 | 13/15 | +6 |
+| Time to first byte | (similar) | (similar) | — |
+| Lines of code | 60 | 850 | +790 (modular) |
+
+The "after" version has more code, but it's modular (10 components vs 1 monolith), testable, accessible, and consistent. The "before" version is short but unmaintainable.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+```bash
+cd examples/01-saas-landing
+# Follow prompts in order: 02 → 03 → 05 → 06 → 07
+# Each prompt is designed to be used with the corresponding skill
+```
